+ For $ee^(-x^2)$, $lim_(x->oo) e^(-x^2)/(e^(-x)) = 0$ and $integral_0^oo ee^(-x) dif x = 1 < oo$, so by the limiting case above,

$
  integral_0^oo ee^(-x^2) dif x < oo.
$

+ $integral_1^oo (x)/(x^4 + 1) dif x$ converges: since

$
  lim_(x->oo) ((x)/(x^4 + 1))/(x^3) = 1 in (0, oo)
$

and $integral_1^oo (1)/(x^3) dif x < oo$, the ratio test gives $integral_1^oo (x)/(x^4 + 1) dif x < oo$.
